course: dictionary
lesson: 13695
title: Inscribed: written or carved on
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Inscribed is the past form of the verb inscribe. When something is inscribed, words or pictures have been written, carved or printed on it, often on stone, metal or the inside of a book. The clue is in how the word is used, and you can check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence.
explain: «The names of the soldiers are inscribed on the war memorial.» Names on a memorial are cut into stone so they last for many years, not just written in pencil. Inscribed must mean carved or written on.
explain: Maths uses the word in a different way. «A circle is inscribed in a square» means the circle is drawn inside the square and just touches each of its sides. The word still points to something inside or on something else.
fact: Inscribe is the verb. Inscribed is its past form, and it can also be used as an adjective.
fact: «Inscribed» means written, carved or printed on something, especially stone, metal or the inside of a book.
fact: In history, names and dates are often inscribed on war memorials and old stones.
fact: In geometry, an inscribed circle touches each side of a triangle or square from the inside.
fact: Words that go with inscribed include «inscribed on», «inscribed with» and «inscribed in a circle».
exercise: «The old coin had a king's face and a year inscribed on its edge.» What does inscribed mean here? | Hidden under the sand | Folded in half | Blown away by the wind | *Carved or printed on it
exercise: «The gate was inscribed with the words Welcome Home.» Where were the words? | Under the sea | *On the gate | In the garden | In the sky
exercise: Maths: «Draw a circle inscribed in a square.» What does inscribed mean in maths? | Doubled in size | Drawn outside, far away from the shape | Coloured in with pencil | *Drawn inside, just touching its sides
test: «Her name was inscribed inside the cover of the old book.» Where was her name? | *Inside the cover of the book | On a bus ticket | Outside in the rain | Under the bed
test: Maths: An inscribed polygon has what? | All its corners far outside the circle | *All its corners touching a circle | Only one side | No corners at all
exam: «The words inscribed on the stone were too worn to read.» What does inscribed mean? | Eaten by animals | Sold at the market | *Carved or written on it | Tied with string
